// P3I.8 / X7, exercise E3 "Drawings" end to end (`ex3-drawings/goal.png`, step-02–12) on its
// stand-in document (`fixtures/sheetmetal/sm_e3_standin.cadrs`: the Sheet Metal Box, the
// exercise's sloped enclosure, material inside: 200 wide, 250 deep, 200 high at the back and 125
// at the front, a 75 deep shelf, the slope left open and a 35 mm flange folded in along each
// sloping edge; 1.5 mm, R1.5, seven bends, all DOWN, two oblique in the flat).
// 01 the box; 01b the Sheet metal table and flat view, right-click on the flat: New sketch,
// Export DXF/DWG of flat pattern, Create drawing of flat pattern (SM14.1, SM15.1, SM16.1);
// 01c Export DXF/DWG of flat pattern (step 2–3); 02 Parts list → Create drawing (the tab
// "Sheet Metal Box Drawing 1"); 03 ANSI_A MM, Four views; 04–05 `step-06`'s dimensions (the
// top view's 200, 75 and 35, the front's 125, the side's 23.2° and 200); 06–08 Insert
// sheet, Insert view → Flat patterns ("Flat pattern of Sheet Metal Box") at 1:5 (1:4 doesn't
// fit beside this template's title block), View orientation → Rotate 90° so the strip stands
// with the front at the top as `goal.png`; its bend notes along the lines (tangent edges hidden:
// clean chain lines); 09–10 bend notes dragged off (leaders stay on their attach points) and
// one dropped back; 11 `goal.png`'s five dimensions, clear of the notes (the strip's width, its
// length 642.25, the side's bottom to the strip's end, the side's reach and the 113.2° at the
// flange); 12 Hide bend notes; 13 undo. The flat is 642.249 × 659.939
// (`cadrs_core/tests/sheetmetal_exercises.rs`, closed forms).
